{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/74556-how-organized-is-demon-society","id":74556,"title":"How organized is Demon society?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-18T14:25:21-08:00","id":74556,"title":"How organized is Demon society?","content":"How would you guys run Demon society? Are the Agencies as organized as, say, Requiem Covenants? Maybe no more organized than the various Geist krewes? Would there be some kind of ultimate authority figure or figures in a given city, or dk demons just not trust anyone enough for that kind of thing? For anyone running a game, how are you doing it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T15:00:40-08:00","id":74578,"title":"","content":"It's more akin to Krewes. Hell, it's really more loose(and carefully watched) networks than an actual structure for each.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T15:22:45-08:00","id":74595,"title":"","content":"My take is that demon society isn't <i>organized</i> so much as it is <i>connected</i>. Demons have links to other demons, but less often an idea of society as a whole. Agendas are broad categories of viewpoint which an intelligent observer can discern, rather than religions or political parties. Agencies vary dramatically in their level of hierarchy: some are vast networks of demonic friendships and (dis)loyalties, whereas others are formal organizations with well-defined rules and ways to communicate as a group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 02-18-2014, 07:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T15:38:58-08:00","id":74604,"title":"","content":"Well.... it depends. The default Unchained society seems to be like Geist or Werewolf - groups of packs/krewes/rings that happen to get along. <br /> <br /> Then, there are Agencies. Even the agencies seem to be fairly informal. <br /> <br /> All in all, it seems that, unlike the hyper organized Angels, demons tend to be pretty individual. Which ties back into the whole Order versus Chaos theme I notice between angels and demons. Security versus Freedom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T17:05:03-08:00","id":74645,"title":"","content":"Yeah, my take is that it's a lot like the cell structure of Hunter. You might know a couple of demons outside of your ring in a personal way but mostly Demon &quot;society&quot; works through a list of phone numbers, emails and dead drops. There might be territory or specific things claimed by specific demons, but I imagine it's mostly a matter of hearsay and it's less enforced and more handled as a gentleman's agreement not to mess with each other's stuff.<br /> <br /> In contrast, Agencies are shining beacons of &quot;society&quot;, organizations based on encouraging interaction and cooperation between the Unchained. By default in my games, this is seen as something to be wary of, groups that are seen as either naive enough to think everyone's going to get along selflessly or manipulative and ruthless enough to embroil everyone in their schemes. Those perceptions plus the fact that it's relatively easy to track down info on Agencies mean it's usually seen as entirely too open to being suborned by the God-Machine and only a resource you should use when there are no easy alternatives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 02-19-2014, 03:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T18:00:32-08:00","id":74690,"title":"","content":"As organized as a group of paranoid, hunted rebels can be, really.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of it as largely a word-of-mouth kind of thing with no meetings larger than 5 or 10, max. <br /> There may be some demons who represent agendas who go around convincing demons to work towards a certain viewpoint but there's certainly no elysium, no council of elders, no &quot;prince&quot; but perhaps a very powerful demon in the region whom others may defer to (or compete against). That said, most demons probably have never met each other instead trading on reputations, stories and notable habits. Any and all of which may suddenly and irrevocably change.<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, great, Ms. Aigh got a couple of her demonic arms torn off by that hunter angel. How are we going to fix it, Bee?&quot;<br /> &quot;Let me see about that... I remember hearing about this demon who worked in a restoration centre before he fell... Or he was a restoration centre - I don't quite remember. Anyway, apparently he's the best thing we have that's close to a surgeon.... or Frankenstein.... Last I heard, I think he was in Canada, maybe. Let's see if he can re-attach it or knows of another way to fix it.&quot;<br /> &quot;Canada? Canada's a big fucking country, Bee anything more specific?&quot;<br /> &quot;Well, here's the thing, Mr. Sea. I think he's a Tempter and I know a Tempter in Toronto who might be able to help us get in touch. No promises though.<br /> &quot;Ugh, any other options?&quot;<br /> &quot;Nope, not unless you want to haul an unconscious Aigh through 'bout five miles of infrastructure...&quot;<br /> &quot;-Sigh- well guess it's a road trip then...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1930-rixx","name":"Rixx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T19:04:49-08:00","id":74718,"title":"","content":"Cute Rixx. <br /> I'd run a Demon society however it worked with the chronicle or city I was running? If I want a big brother like feel maybe do something akin to mage, especially if there is a large G-M or Angel presence (or a fabricated one) and another watchful eye if for your own good. <br /> Keep it as loose as Promethean with rings scattered across something the size of new york and everyone just trying to cut a piece of the pie for themselves.<br /> Or it could be a city that's like an active war zone. With rings protecting/ fighting territories and having to run lines of communication by every changing means. Where rings keep in touch but never meet by more than proxies and even then setting something up could take weeks in which valuable time and resources are lost. Where every attempt to talk to an alley is just another risk and blowing your position. It's madness! <br /> Or you know, mix it up as the story progresses.<br /> On the forums someone used the phrase something like &quot;Exactly one metric plot&quot; for the amount of Angels. I think that fits nicely with Demon society. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T04:40:19-08:00","id":74889,"title":"","content":"All this said... Tempters are probably the most likely to have an organization going strong. After all, they're the ones who believe that they have to literally build Hell, and that requires pooling resources. They're the ones most likely to call for a unified Demon society, or establish a pecking order. Their drive does need some stronger organization than the rest, I think, despite the risks.<br /> <br /> On the opposite side of the equation, I see Interrogators being the least organized of the lot. They don't even trust each other with the information they gather. Their version of Hell is something that can only be achieved by individuals, instead of groups. So, while you might have a ring of Interrogators that might have the equivalent to a Buddhist temple, this temple will have no official organization or ties to another Interrogator &quot;temple&quot; in another part of the same city. Maybe a nod in passing. Or perhaps note passing when they need to work on a large project that benefits many of their number. But they have the least benefit when operating together.<br /> <br /> Integrators and Saboteurs probably fit somewhere between. They benefit from working together, but growing bigger undermines their organization's goal more than helps. Monolithic Saboteur armies are prone to infiltration and being taken down easily, so they need to have discrete cells that wage war and won't bring down the whole if its damaged. Integrators benefit from sharing information and working together to jack in and other attempts to do the whole Exile thing, but again are prone to being broken when someone messes up and just has all their memories downloaded by a hunter angel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T15:55:25-08:00","id":323913,"title":"","content":"I actually gave my players a rundown as to how the clandestine cell system works as a general rule, and how it could be applied to Unchained Rings. Looking it up on Wikipedia is really cool, and it seems like the Unchained would set up their Ring structures in such a way that they can minimize the chance and effectiveness of compromise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4392-vaermithrax","name":"vaermithrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T09:01:05-08:00","id":326080,"title":"","content":"My reading of it is that Demons just don't trust each other enough to have anything too organised. What works is a set of groups who largely keep to themselves, often forming out of necessity rather than a desire to be with others and who only see each other when there's work to be done. Anything bigger is likely a cult of personality or has formed out of a greater need (I'm toying with character gen and have a character who would very much like to form an agency but isn't in a position to do so).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4404-steve_cotterill","name":"steve_cotterill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}